  "reply_markdown": "**Q1.** Neither proposed order unchanged. Start with a pinned v0.6.1 contract/test inventory, then A/C/D, B+F together, G+E together, shared plan scheduling/health, and finally H’s authenticated execution paths. Keep one worker per wave; split the larger waves into separately reviewed commits. Recovery classification and release rules belong together; new rating events need a durable spool. H-first is reasonable only as an experimental vertical slice if Claude availability is the immediate operator priority. I need that priority, release deadline, and permitted compatibility exceptions to choose.\n\nChallenge the framing: define a **compatibility release** and a separately measured **improvement track**. A passing legacy harness, a native API response, and a better review are three different outcomes.\n\n**Q2.** Ship spawned Claude Code for all three plugin auth modes first; add native Messages as an explicit HTTP transport afterward. A third option is retaining the existing Codex endpoint route while comparing both alternatives. Do not silently reinterpret `engine: claude` as HTTP or resume CLI sessions through native replay.\n\nNative loses adaptive repository discovery, tool evidence, Claude session/fork semantics, and CLI-specific proof and quota events. Packs can compensate for bounded reviews, but omitted dependencies require an explicit insufficient-evidence result or another pack round. `[1m]` is a CLI model convention, not proof of native context capacity; negotiate and budget against the endpoint’s actual limit. Treat unavailable quota signals as unknown, never unlimited. The plugin’s 3–6× result compares Codex with Claude Code, not native Messages (finding #8). Choose using plan access, blind review quality, omission rate, credits, latency, and retry rates.\n\n**Q3.** Keep shared recovery and health authoritative in compatible files. Keep SurrealDB derived: its documented exclusive process lifetime conflicts with concurrent operational use. A separate transactional outbox, SQLite store, or single-writer service is an option for C3-only telemetry, provided its durability and forgetting behavior are specified. File exports alone cannot provide shared locking authority. First establish whether compatibility includes machine-wide state and salt/instance identity across bridges; `.collab` compatibility alone leaves that undecided.\n\n**Q4.** Run pinned harnesses sequentially: especially fixes28e, fixes28d, telemetry, claude, roster, panel, pending, fixes, lock2, detach, and ledger-order checks in 0.3/engines/muse/companions. Classify each assertion as C3 execution, PowerShell-helper-only, or documentation; port helper-only cases to Rust. Add the missing telemetry shim.\n\nLive: Codex, Antigravity, Muse, Claude subscription, API-key, and each claimed endpoint plan; retain HTTP coverage. Missing credentials mean explicitly unverified modes. Observe model/auth identity, usable schema, read-only enforcement, continuation/fork, timeout recovery, and redaction. A mixed panel must show required seats, light fallback, independent consultation references, shared-plan serialization across repositories, quota propagation, reconciled ledger entries, and no surviving children. Repeat core recovery tests on Linux and test both feature configurations.\n\n**Q5.** Correct E: commit-before-spool already exists; revision/judge/backfill durability does not. D’s anchor is absent. Expand A’s fixtures to yesterday near midnight and whole-token malformed offsets. Extract global `plan` semantics from H. Add spool lost-update, telemetry classifier, and failed-forget cases (findings #1–3). The shim document’s missing-`ScriptsDir` claim is obsolete; pinned v0.6.1 supports it.\n\n## Requested checks\n\n- **RC1:** CWD repository root; workspace-write; run deterministic local-intake fixtures for findings #1–3: pause flush, append, release; serialize private labels; fail DELETE then retry. Settle loss, disclosure, and retained deletion identity; budget 30 minutes.\n- **RC2:** CWD repository root; workspace-write; build the pinned harness staging directory, run all 22 harnesses sequentially, and map each assertion to its executing implementation. Settle oracle coverage; budget two hours.\n- **RC3:** CWD isolated scratch repositories; workspace-write plus provider access; execute Q4’s engine and mixed-panel matrix, alternating plugin/C3 writes on one task. Settle live and interchange compatibility; budget two hours.\n- **RC4:** CWD isolated benchmark repository; workspace-write plus metered provider access; compare Codex, Claude endpoint, and native Messages on 12 randomized paired briefs per plan with blind grading. Settle finding #8; budget 36 calls per plan plus fixed retry allowance.",
